1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,839
In the 8th century, an Indian Queen made a vow that should have killed her.

2
00:00:05,839 --> 00:00:09,343
Her husband, the King, recovered from a deadly illness.

3
00:00:09,343 --> 00:00:17,129
In gratitude, she vowed to fast to death until she could see the pinnacle of a temple built for Shiva.

4
00:00:17,129 --> 00:00:23,357
Royal architects told the king: 'It will take twenty years to build from the ground up.

5
00:00:23,357 --> 00:00:33,090
The Queen will starve.' Then one architect named Kokasa stepped forward with an engineering heresy: 'I will show you the spire in seven days.' How?

6
00:00:33,090 --> 00:00:35,815
Every builder built from the ground up.

7
00:00:35,815 --> 00:00:40,487
He decided to climb the mountain and carve downward from the clouds!

8
00:00:40,487 --> 00:00:45,158
In seven days, the queen saw the pinnacle and broke her fast.

9
00:00:45,158 --> 00:00:51,776
Beneath it lay four hundred thousand tons of solid rock that became the world's greatest monolithic temple.

10
00:00:51,776 --> 00:00:59,951
Watch Episode One of our full documentary series linked below to see how this impossible plan was actually funded and engineered!

